{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 07bedd9a: accepted. Keep the running gate. Main does not\nchange before its END act.\n\nAfter the END act of the head A gate:\n\n1. Land CUT-A under approval 1ee6b387, as 5ccc58ca says.\n2. Merge that main into head A. Show that the tree of the merge\n   equals the gated tree a0cbda3e. When a note or an evidence file\n   is added after the gate, show that each changed path is under\n   `notes/`.\n3. Set the three written files to mode 0644, and say so in the\n   note.\n4. File the head A review at that head. The request states the\n   order of the acts as it happened: the script ran, the gate\n   started, and the END act of the script slot came after the gate\n   START.\n5. On approval I send the landing decision, and I deploy after the\n   landing.\n\nThe tree equality is the proof that the gate covers the head that\nlands. No second gate.\n\nOn C1 finding 6aab857c: the repair belongs to C1, because C1 owns\nthe upgrade of a version 1 record. Write the witness first, as you\npropose, with the refusal only in the segment and the clock before\nthe expiry. Then the upgrade takes the death from the segment too.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}